\id PHM - The Text-Critical English New Testament
\h THE LETTER OF PAUL TO PHILEMON
\toc1 The Letter of Paul to Philemon
\toc2 Philemon
\toc3 Philem.
\mt2 THE LETTER OF PAUL TO
\mt1 PHILEMON
\c 1
\s1 Greeting
\m
\v 1 Paul, a prisoner for \f + \fr 1:1 \fq Jesus Christ \ft 54.5% ¦ Christ Jesus ANT CT HF RP TR 45.2% \f*Jesus Christ, and Timothy our brother, to Philemon, our beloved friend and fellow worker,
\v 2 and also to \f + \fr 1:2 \fq the beloved \ft 93.4% ¦ our sister CT 5.4%\f*the beloved Apphia, to Archippus our fellow soldier, and to the church that meets in yoʋr house:
\v 3 Grace to you and peace from God our Father and the Lord Jesus Christ.
\s1 Philemon's Love and Faith
\m
\v 4 I give thanks to my God, always making mention of yoʋ in my prayers,
\v 5 because I hear of yoʋr love for all the saints and the faith that yoʋ have toward the Lord Jesus.
\v 6 I pray that yoʋr fellowship with us in the faith may be effective in deepening yoʋr understanding of every blessing that \f + \fr 1:6 \fq we \ft 64.4% ¦ you PCK TR 34.7%\f*we have in Christ \f + \fr 1:6 \fq Jesus \ft 96.6% ¦ — CT 2.1%\f*Jesus.
\v 7 \f + \fr 1:7 \fq We are very thankful for the comfort we have received \ft 76.2% ¦ We have received much joy and comfort ELZ SCR 4.8% ¦ I have received much joy and comfort CT 4.1%\f*We are very thankful for the comfort we have received from yoʋr love, because the hearts of the saints have been refreshed through yoʋ, brother.
\s1 Paul's Appeal for Onesimus
\m
\v 8 Therefore, although I am bold enough in Christ to command yoʋ to do what is right,
\v 9 I would rather appeal to yoʋ on the basis of love. I, Paul, an old man and now a prisoner for \f + \fr 1:9 \fq Jesus Christ \ft 91.9% ¦ Christ Jesus CT 6.1%\f*Jesus Christ,
\v 10 appeal to yoʋ on behalf of my child, Onesimus, whose father I have become during my imprisonment.
\v 11 Once he was useless to yoʋ, but now he is useful both to yoʋ and to me. I am sending him \f + \fr 1:11 \fq back \ft 93.1% ¦ back to yoʋ CT 0.7%\f*back,
\v 12 \f + \fr 1:12 \fq and I ask yoʋ to receive him, \ft 91.6% ¦ — CT 0.9%\f*and I ask yoʋ to receive him, that is, my very own heart.
\v 13 I wanted to keep him with me so that he could serve me in yoʋr place during my imprisonment for the gospel.
\v 14 But I did not want to do anything without yoʋr consent, so that yoʋr good deed would not be done out of compulsion but of yoʋr own free will.
\v 15 Perhaps the reason he was separated from yoʋ for an hour was so that yoʋ might have him back forever,
\v 16 no longer as a slave, but more than a slave, as a beloved brother, especially to me, but even more so to yoʋ, both in the flesh and in the Lord.
\p
\v 17 So if yoʋ consider me to be a partner, receive him as yoʋ would receive me.
\v 18 If he has wronged yoʋ in any way or owes yoʋ anything, charge it to me.
\v 19 I, Paul, write this with my own hand: I will repay it (not to mention that yoʋ owe me yoʋr very own life).
\v 20 Yes, brother, let me have some benefit from yoʋ in the Lord. Refresh my heart in \f + \fr 1:20 \fq the Lord \ft 74.4% ¦ Christ CT 20.3%\f*the Lord.
\p
\v 21 Trusting in yoʋr obedience, I write to yoʋ, knowing that yoʋ will do even more than I ask.
\v 22 At the same time, I want yoʋ to prepare a guest room for me, for I hope that through your prayers I will be restored to you soon.
\s1 Final Greetings
\m
\v 23 Epaphras, my fellow prisoner in Christ \f + \fr 1:23 \fq Jesus, and Mark, Aristarchus, Demas, and Luke, my fellow workers, greet yoʋ. \ft 72.8% ¦ Jesus greets yoʋ, and so do Mark, Aristarchus, Demas, and Luke, my fellow workers. ANT CT 25.5%\f*Jesus,
\v 24 and Mark, Aristarchus, Demas, and Luke, my fellow workers, greet yoʋ.
\p
\v 25 The grace of \f + \fr 1:25 \fq our \ft 89.4% ¦ the NA SBL WH 6.7%\f*our Lord Jesus \f + \fr 1:25 \fq Christ \ft 80% ¦ — PCK 15.9%\f*Christ be with your spirit.
\d \f + \fr 1:25 \fq Amen. \ft 91.2% ¦ — NA SBL WH 2.3%\f*Amen.
